statement:
For every n ≥ 1 there is C > 0 such that for every ε' > 0 there is δ_h > 0 with the following property. Let R₀ > 0 and let w : ℝⁿ → ℝ (ℝⁿ = Euclid n) be Lipschitz with ∫_{B̆_{R₀}(0)} ‖Dw‖² ≤ R₀ⁿ. Suppose |∫_{B̆_{R₀}(0)} Σ_i ∂_iw·∂_iζ| ≤ δ_hR₀ⁿG for every C¹ function ζ : ℝⁿ → ℝ with compact support and tsupport ζ ⊆ B̆_{R₀}(0), and every G ∈ ℝ with ‖Dζ(v)‖ ≤ G for all v. Here Dw = fderiv ℝ w, ∂_iw = Dw(e_i), e_i = EuclideanSpace.single i 1, and the integrals are over the open ball. Then there are a ∈ ℝ and a continuous linear functional b : ℝⁿ → ℝ with:
- ‖b‖ ≤ C;
- |a| ≤ C·√((∫_{B̆_{R₀}(0)} w²)/R₀ⁿ) + C·√ε'·R₀;
- ∫_{B̆_{θ'R₀}(0)} (w(v) − a − b(v))² dv ≤ C(ε'/θ'^{n+2} + θ'²)(θ'R₀)^{n+2} for every θ' ∈ (0, 1/4].
This is harmonic approximation with affine decay: Simon Ch. 5, Lemma 3.1 with the estimates 3.2–3.4. (The frozen Lean type is character-identical to that of DAG node root.density_one_implies_regular-a1.epsilon_regularity-a1.allard_graph-a1.harmonic_approximation-a1, dorag_harmonic_affine_approximation, which is not yet comparator-accepted. It is declared here under the fresh name Submission.dimred_cdg_harmonic_affine_approximation.)
